  "prefLabel": "Ch 407.08 Obligation to Report Certain Complaints to the Board",
  "priorExpiration": "2017-08-20",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ch 407.08 Obligation to Report Certain Complaints to the Board. A licensee shall report to the board a complaint made against the licensee in any court or in any professional or business organization of which the licensee is a member:\n\n(a) As soon as the licensee becomes aware of the complaint; and\n\n(b) In answering the question in Ch 402.05(p), on the licensee's license-renewal application form.\n\nSource. #8739, eff 10-11-06, EXPIRED 10-11-14\n\nNew. #12107, INTERIM, eff 2-21-17, EXPIRED: 8-20-17\n\nNew. #12431, eff 12-8-17; renumbered by #13327 (formerly Ch 406.08) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Ch 400)",
